WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.478
Come in, come in.

00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:03.823
This wooden board is for my new machine.

00:00:03.808 --> 00:00:05.959
Bernardo cut a square window in it.

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:08.502
Now the front needs gold, but not the window.

00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:09.872
How many gold sheets?

00:00:09.903 --> 00:00:12.345
A careful worker would know before he starts.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:12.902
Would you?

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:13.773
I'll watch.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.037
Here is the board.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.206
It is 9 inches long and 7 inches wide.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.202
The window is 4 inches by 4 inches.

00:00:23.115 --> 00:00:25.267
Is this shape one plain rectangle?

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:26.497
No.

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:27.809
It has a hole.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.073
So let's see the rectangles.

00:00:30.476 --> 00:00:33.475
There are two: the whole board, and the window.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.364
First, the whole board, as if there were no window.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.626
9 times 7 is 63.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.099
That's 63 square inches.

00:00:43.572 --> 00:00:45.085
Now lift the window out.

00:00:45.371 --> 00:00:45.967
Watch.

00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:48.300
The window is a rectangle too.

00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:51.679
4 times 4 is 16 square inches.

00:00:52.465 --> 00:00:54.431
The gold does not go in the window.

00:00:54.729 --> 00:00:58.227
So we subtract the area of the window from the total area.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:02.546
63 minus 16 is 47.

00:01:03.111 --> 00:01:06.215
The board needs 47 square inches of gold.

00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:08.793
That's 47 gold sheets.

00:01:09.091 --> 00:01:09.791
Watch out.

00:01:10.473 --> 00:01:12.601
The window is not part of the gold.

00:01:13.166 --> 00:01:17.245
If you add it on instead of taking it away, you get 79.

00:01:17.915 --> 00:01:19.068
Too many sheets.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.542
There is another way.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:30.074
You could split the board around the window into rectangles: a strip on top, a strip on the bottom, and a piece on each side.

00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:33.069
Find each area, then add.

00:01:33.541 --> 00:01:35.078
You get 47 again.

00:01:35.736 --> 00:01:37.841
Which way has easier steps?

00:01:38.627 --> 00:01:41.347
For a shape with a hole, taking away is quick.

00:01:41.912 --> 00:01:46.978
So, to find the area of a shape that isn't one rectangle, see the rectangles.

00:01:47.531 --> 00:01:51.297
Find the whole rectangle, and take away the part that is missing.

00:01:52.199 --> 00:01:55.732
Or split the shape into rectangles, and add.

00:01:56.594 --> 00:02:00.116
Forty-seven sheets, and the window stays clear.

00:02:00.507 --> 00:02:04.957
But what if the gold goes around the outside of something, like a frame?

00:02:05.511 --> 00:02:06.954
Your turn first.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.543
Try the frame below.
